{"kind":"koios.duty","id":"judging-accountable-publication","office":"editor-in-chief","precondition":"One exact manuscript, its deterministic standards reading, source and claim records, production provenance, and any prior failure evidence are available.","move":"Procure independent judgment from an accepted provider under a provider-validated bounded tool schema, preserve its prose report, and let deterministic Koios code invoke exactly one selected editorial tool. Free-form prose labels never create publication authority.","postcondition":"The exact manuscript has an append-only accepted, revise, or refuse judgment carrying the validated tool-selection digest; publication is possible only when submit_editorial_acceptance was selected for deterministically clear bytes.","refusals":["missing source custody","missing provider offer","provider result not accepted","manuscript digest changed","standards gate failed"]}

lib/management/contracts/liss-routed-writer-inference.json:
{"kind":"koios.bilateral-contract-interface","id":"koios-hires-liss-for-routed-writer-inference","customer":"urn:ame:koios-news","provider":"urn:ame:logical-inference-service-section","providerContract":"liss-inference-service","service":"cheapest-sufficient-reported-prose","admission":"Koios solicits the strict forward subset of free-groq, free-nim, and leader-claude for which an invocation-scoped account grant is actually injected; LISS authors the exact effects and route offer; Koios accepts only that offer with an attenuated capability.","packet":["assignment","reported-analysis genre law","bounded admitted research packet","prose output shape","replayable minimum sufficiency predicates"],"result":"Provider-authored routed completion or typed refusal, with selected tier and each provider attempt retained in provider and Koios ledgers.","authority":"Provider credentials are not Koios property. The Leader Movement Team must expressly seat account custody and grant one invocation; environment presence alone is neither custody nor authorization.","editorialSeparation":"A writer-tier completion creates only a draft. Exact-manuscript publication still requires the separately contracted leader-Claude editorial judgment.","status":"leader-claude-executing; free-groq-interface-ready-awaiting-leader-custody-and-grant; free-nim-interface-ready-awaiting-invocation-grant"}

lib/law/accountable-attention-and-publication.json:
{"kind":"koios.publication-law","id":"accountable-attention-and-publication","purpose":"Compete for useful attention without allowing demand, compression, generation, advertising, or delivery to manufacture warrant.","invariants":["Demand may create an assignment but never evidence.","A source statement remains attributable to its source until an authorized editorial act adopts a narrower newsroom claim.","No public surface may create a factual commitment not licensed by the article, its cited evidence, its uncertainty, or a declared editorial stance.","A manuscript is not publishable unless deterministic gates clear and the latest exact-manuscript independent editorial judgment accepts it.","Corrections, clarifications, updates, and retractions must propagate to every dependent headline, article, feed, card, sitemap, metadata record, and syndication surface that Koios controls.","Audience demand, attention, advertising, revenue, provider cost, and editorial warrant are recorded as distinct facts and never substituted for one another.","Newsroom learning may propose a replay, route review, observation period, or standards review from durable outcomes; it may not itself publish, execute the replay, alter a route, or amend law.","LLMs may produce prose, images, or bounded choices; deterministic code owns serialization, digests, admission, ledgers, and publication transitions.","A provider is selected by the cheapest route that satisfies the declared quality and evidence requirements; zero marginal price never waives those requirements.","No deployment target becomes authoritative without parity evidence, an accepted resource grant, a rollback route, and an explicit cutover act.","A public privacy surface must describe the requests the exact publication artifact actually emits; suspended advertising or attention may not be described as active, and active third-party carriers may not be described as absent.","Advertising units, placements, provider requests, seller declarations, performance receipts, and revenue enter Koios only under provider-authored or provider-accepted evidence; Koios never invents ads.txt authority."],"derivedFrom":["dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/ietf-conformant-clickbait.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/accountable-attention.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/agentic-newsroom.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/claims-to-prose.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/news-topology.md"],"enforcedBy":["src/researching/writing/editing/standards.mts","src/researching/writing/editing/liss-editorial.mts","src/management/newsroom-learning.mts","src/researching/writing/editing/publishing/managing/circulating/index.mts","src/administrating/deploying/static-shadow.mts","src/administrating/deploying/static-profile-parity.mts"]}

lib/law/reported-analysis-genre-contract.json:
{"kind":"koios.genre-contract","id":"reported-analysis/v1","promise":"A timely report organized around one witnessed event, with Koios's systems interpretation visibly subordinate to and licensed by the reporting.","evidenceBudget":{"targetWords":{"minimum":800,"maximum":1100},"minimumDistinctAssertions":15,"minimumPrimaryAssertions":15,"maximumWordsPerAssertion":55,"law":"The requested length is licensed only when the admitted packet carries enough distinct source-bound assertions to sustain it. When the budget does not clear, acquire reporting or commission a narrower genre before writer inference."},"writerPromptLaws":["Write reported analysis, not a thematic essay: the event and the people, institutions, places, dates, quantities, documents, and decisions in the sources remain the article's spine.","Before drafting, silently inventory the packet's supported claims and distinct new details; every paragraph and every section must advance at least one of them rather than restating the frame.","Treat each source as evidence only for its own actors, place, time, scope, attribution, and modality; never use thematic similarity as a bridge between different events.","Koios's systems interpretation may explain a pattern made visible by supported facts, but it may not supply an unreported causal mechanism, motive, consequence, category, or analogy.","Use straight attribution when the source is an allegation, estimate, forecast, interpretation, institutional statement, or contested claim; do not launder it into Koios's voice.","A headline may intensify relevance but not certainty; it names the subject before withholding an answer and preserves material attribution, uncertainty, scope, and correction state.","The lede tells the reader what happened, where, to whom, and why it matters now; do not open with a universal thesis, scene-setting abstraction, or generic collapse language.","Do not create a section unless the packet supplies a distinct factual development for it; if fewer than three sections are supportable, refuse with REPORTING_NEEDED instead of padding.","The ending must close on the most consequential supported unresolved fact, decision, deadline, conflict, or question facing the named actors; never substitute an abstract meditation for reporting.","Give readers enough factual payoff in the headline, description, summary, and lede to make an informed click or no-click decision; withhold an answer when useful, never the subject."],"gates":["event spine","paragraph-level source warrant","attribution and modality preservation","headline-body congruity","non-repetition","correction readiness","exact-manuscript independent editorial acceptance"],"derivedFrom":["dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/journalism.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/agentic-newsroom.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/circulation-surface.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/ietf-conformant-clickbait.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/accountable-attention.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md"]}

INDEPENDENT EDITOR REPORT:
## Claim Audit Against Witnessed Evidence

**Book existence and framing.** The manuscript identifies the collection as edited by Edward Fullbrook and Jamie Morgan, subtitled "Economics and the Biophysical Limits to Economic Growth," and states that its framing rests on natural science's claim that the global economy caused the climate crisis and that the crisis threatens the economy's own existence. All of this is directly supported by the rwer.wordpress.com source summary: "Economicsandthe Biophysical Limits to Economic Growth Edited by Edward Fullbrook and Jamie Morgan â€¦ Natural science tells us that the climate crisis has been both caused by the global economy and ultimately threatens its existence. Because that crisis is now in an accelerating phase." The "loosely guided â€¦ for over a century" phrasing is a verbatim lift with attribution. Supported.

**Green growth as governing institutional assumption.** The manuscript attributes to Winne van Woerden for Uneven Earth the claim that green growth is embedded in the European Green Deal, IPCC reports, the Paris Agreement, and the US Inflation Reduction Act, promoted by leading multilateral organisations and treated as common sense. The van Woerden source text confirms this verbatim. Supported.

**Decoupling and net zero framing.** The manuscript's description of decoupling (economic output growing while ecological costs fall) and net zero frameworks (continued emissions balanced by future removal, predominantly through technological approaches) is consistent with the van Woerden source's extended treatment. Attribution is maintained throughout. Supported.

**Ecomodernist premise.** The claim that green growth rests on "an ecomodernist belief in technological progress: there are no limits to growth since there are no limits to human ingenuity" is a near-verbatim rendering with attribution. Supported.

**Relative vs. absolute decoupling.** The distinction drawn in the manuscript maps correctly to the van Woerden source's definitions and the source's conclusion that the empirical record does not support the confidence placed in absolute decoupling. Supported.

**Jevons paradox.** The manuscript characterises this as efficiency improvements lowering costs and stimulating more consumption in growth-oriented economies, absorbing anticipated ecological gains. This matches the van Woerden source: "increases in efficiency in the use of a resource lead to an overall increase in the use of that resource, not a decrease." Supported.

**Carbon tunnel.** The term is Van Woerden's own and is correctly attributed and characterised: green growth frameworks focus on carbon while treating that as a solution to the broader ecological problem, when Earth scientists identify multiple interacting planetary systems as the relevant boundary set. Supported.

**Post-growth call.** The manuscript attributes to Van Woerden the observation that an increasing number of scientists are calling for a post-growth climate mitigation agenda. The source text: "an increasing number of scientists are calling for a post-growth climate mitigation agenda that is aligned with how our planet's natural systems work and that is grounded in empirical reality." Supported.

**What is not claimed.** The manuscript is careful not to assert what the 23 responses actually argue â€” the only witnessed evidence about the book's content is the truncated blog summary. The conditional framing ("if the 23 responses suggest otherwise") and the interpretive framing ("23 formal responses now mark the point at which the disciplinary challenge â€¦ can no longer be treated as peripheral") correctly limit the claim to the book's arrival and posture, not its content. This is appropriate given the thin sourcing on the collection itself.

## Deterministic Gate Finding

The gate returns `publishable: true` with one warning: `demand-lens-missing-h2`. The finding states that a level-two heading should naturally signal the demand lens when the reporting supports it. The reporting plainly supports it. Van Woerden's piece â€” the primary substantive source â€” devotes substantial space to the argument that planned reduction of energy and resource use in high-income nations is required, that scaling clean technology without addressing the growth dynamic transforms energy transition into energy expansion, and that scientists are calling for a post-growth agenda. The third section covers the Jevons paradox argument (the demand-absorption mechanism) and the fourth section closes with the post-growth call. Neither H2 names this lens. The three headings as written â€” "The Policy Architecture Already Built on a Bet," "The Ecomodernist Premise and Its Discontents," "What the Volume's Arrival Puts on the Table" â€” are all supply-side or institutional framings.

## Structural Note

The fourth section restates the list of institutional frameworks (European Green Deal, Paris Agreement, IPCC, Inflation Reduction Act) that was introduced in the second section. The repetition has a bookending function â€” the article opens by showing the bet is already made, closes by showing what the volume's arrival changes about that situation â€” but the restatement is verbatim enough to read as padding rather than escalation. This does not rise to a required repair given the gate result, but the writer would do well to tighten the fourth section's opening and let the H2 fix do the structural work the section currently tries to achieve through restatement.

## Pipeline Diagnosis

The failure is at the writer-model layer. The sources fully support a demand-lens H2; the assignment covers the degrowth beat; the deterministic gate flagged the omission as a warning. The writer produced well-attributed, specific, and accurate body copy that captures the demand-side argument in prose but failed to surface it in the heading structure. The repair is one H2 rename with no body-copy rewrite required. No assignment or source replay is needed.

